+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+  <meta charset="UTF-8">
+  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
+  <title>Visually Stable Mixed Fonts &amp; Theme Typography</title>
+  <style>
+    :root {
+      --bg-page: #f8fafc;
+      --bg-surface: #ffffff;
+      --bg-code: #f1f5f9;
+      --bg-theme-alt: #1e293b;
+      --text-primary: #0f172a;
+      --text-secondary: #475569;
+      --text-code: #0369a1;
+      --text-theme-alt: #f8fafc;
+      --text-theme-alt-muted: #cbd5e1;
+      --border-subtle: #e2e8f0;
+      --border-theme-alt: #334155;
+      --accent: #2563eb;
+    }
+
+    *,
+    *::before,
+    *::after {
+      box-sizing: border-box;
+    }
+
+    body {
+      margin: 0;
+      padding: 2rem 1.25rem;
+      background-color: var(--bg-page);
+      color: var(--text-primary);
+      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
+      font-size: 1rem;
+      line-height: 1.5;
+      text-align: start;
+      overflow-wrap: break-word;
+    }
+
+    main {
+      max-width: 65ch;
+      margin-inline: auto;
+      display: flex;
+      flex-direction: column;
+      gap: 2rem;
+    }
+
+    header h1 {
+      font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.1rem + 2vw, 2.5rem);
+      line-height: 1.2;
+      margin-block: 0 0.5rem;
+      text-wrap: balance;
+    }
+
+    header p {
+      margin-block: 0;
+      color: var(--text-secondary);
+      text-wrap: pretty;
+    }
+
+    h2 {
+      font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 1rem + 1.2vw, 1.75rem);
+      line-height: 1.3;
+      margin-block: 0 0.75rem;
+      text-wrap: balance;
+    }
+
+    p {
+      margin-block: 0 1rem;
+      max-width: 65ch;
+      text-wrap: pretty;
+    }
+
+    p:last-child {
+      margin-block-end: 0;
+    }
+
+    /* 1. Mixed Fonts Container: Automatically normalize visual height using from-font */
+    #mixed-fonts-container {
+      font-family: Verdana, "Segoe UI", system-ui, sans-serif;
+      font-size: 1.0625rem;
+      line-height: 1.6;
+      font-size-adjust: from-font;
+      background-color: var(--bg-surface);
+      border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
+      border-radius: 0.75rem;
+      padding: 1.5rem;
+      box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.06);
+    }
+
+    #mixed-fonts-container code {
+      font-family: "JetBrains Mono", "Fira Code", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
+      background-color: var(--bg-code);
+      color: var(--text-code);
+      padding: 0.125em 0.375em;
+      border-radius: 0.25rem;
+    }
+
+    /* 2. Independent Theme Container: Lock down visual proportions with a specific numeric metric override */
+    #independent-theme-container {
+      font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", Times, serif;
+      font-size: 1.0625rem;
+      line-height: 1.6;
+      font-size-adjust: 0.52;
+      background-color: var(--bg-theme-alt);
+      color: var(--text-theme-alt);
+      border: 1px solid var(--border-theme-alt);
+      border-radius: 0.75rem;
+      padding: 1.5rem;
+      box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.15);
+    }
+
+    #independent-theme-container p {
+      color: var(--text-theme-alt-muted);
+    }
+
+    #independent-theme-container strong {
+      color: var(--text-theme-alt);
+    }
+
+    /* Fallback for browsers without support for font-size-adjust: from-font */
+    @supports not (font-size-adjust: from-font) {
+      #mixed-fonts-container {
+        font-size: 1.05rem;
+        line-height: 1.65;
+      }
+
+      #mixed-fonts-container code {
+        font-size: 0.94em;
+        line-height: 1.5;
+      }
+
+      #independent-theme-container {
+        font-size: 1.125rem;
+        line-height: 1.65;
+      }
+    }
+  </style>
+</head>
+<body>
+  <main>
+    <header>
+      <h1>Normalized Typography Across Mixed Fonts and Themes</h1>
+      <p>
+        Demonstrating automatic visual height normalization with modern CSS font metric adjustments.
+      </p>
+    </header>
+
+    <section id="mixed-fonts-container" aria-labelledby="mixed-fonts-heading">
+      <h2 id="mixed-fonts-heading">Automatic Mixed-Font Normalization</h2>
+      <p>
+        When prose mixes a primary humanist sans-serif typeface with inline code fragments such as
+        <code>const aspectRatio = font.xHeight / font.size;</code> or CSS rules like
+        <code>font-size-adjust: from-font</code>, differences in lowercase x-height can make the inline
+        monospace glyphs appear jarring or disproportionately scaled.
+      </p>
+      <p>
+        By declaring <code>font-size-adjust: from-font</code> on <code>#mixed-fonts-container</code>, the browser
+        automatically extracts the first available font's x-height ratio and scales nested inline
+        <code>&lt;code&gt;</code> elements to match the surrounding text's visual height seamlessly.
+      </p>
+    </section>
+
+    <section id="independent-theme-container" aria-labelledby="independent-theme-heading">
+      <h2 id="independent-theme-heading">Independent Theme with Numeric Metric Override</h2>
+      <p>
+        This standalone editorial callout uses a classic serif font stack with its own independent theme styling.
+        Rather than inheriting font metrics from a parent element, it applies an explicit numeric override of
+        <strong>font-size-adjust: 0.52</strong> to lock down its lowercase x-height to 52% of the em box.
+      </p>
+      <p>
+        Locking the x-height aspect ratio numerically guarantees consistent optical density and legibility even if the
+        underlying serif font swaps across operating systems or fallback typefaces.
+      </p>
+    </section>
+  </main>
+</body>
+</html>

